Hi Kirk,

I did this under 4.0g with no problem.  I added the card and the
system booted just fine.  If you can get by the reboot problem,
once booted, I did the things below.  You might try to
boot -fi genvmunix from the chevron prompt.

 Shutdown and halt to >>>
 >>> boot -fi genvmunix
 #sizer -n newconfig
 Edit /usr/sys/conf/YOURSYSNAME (old config)
 Look at /tmp/newconfig
 Copy new lines from newconfig to YOURSYSNAME
 #doconfig -c YOURSYSNAME
 #mv /vmunix /vmunix.bak
 #mv /sys/YOURSYSNAME/vmunix /vmunix
 Shutdown and reboot (should be using your new kernel with support for
     your new card)
 Then I added the new drives.

Ray

