Since the QuickSpecs claims it is supported, one of three
problems comes to mind:

o  Bad adapter.

o  Bad PCI slot.

o  Bad kernel.

Booting the generic kernel is quickest and easiest (when you can
get the system to reboot it) way to check the last.  If the
generic kernel likes it, odds are it is just a problem of not
having a driver in the current kernel.  The operating system
should behave better when a device without a driver is present,
but V5 changed lots of things and being tolerant seems to have
been one of those.

If the generic kernel has a similar problem with the adapter,
then it suggests a hardware problem.  It could be that the
adapter is sensitive to the slot it is installed in.  Or, it
could just be a bad adapter.

