or base system adapter is.  My recollection is that an "isp" family
controller is what is built-in.  I suspect the KZPCA isn't in this
family, so the existing kernel won't have a driver for it.

For what it is worth, I have a KZPBA installed in my XP1000 (not the
667 Mhz) and it behaves fine.  I don't have anything connected to it
and I'm running V4.0G, but that's something resembling a data point.
