> /usr/var/adm/patch/log
> 
> Look there and you should find an install log from every patch applied to
> the system, as long as someone didn't come along and toast them.

grep KITNAME /var/adm/patch/log/event.log

You should get some lines that look like this:

KITNAME><DUV40DAS0008-20001110> OSF425

To figure out exactly what this means:

DU        = Digital Unix
V         = Version
40D       = 4.0d
AS        = ?? (Aggregate Set?)
0008      = Patchkit 8
20001110  = the date the patchkit was completed (not installed)

