Or set the card's firmware at the srm console prompt, like this:

>>> sho ew*
 (lists all ew* variables; pick out the ew*_mode for your adapter, e.g.
  ewa0_mode, and say)

>>> set ewa0_mode fastfd

  (may take a few seconds to complete)

>>> init

  (never hurts. you *did* set auto_action to halt, didn't you?)



Or append "speed 200" to the IFCONFIG_* line in /etc/rc.config for
your adapter.

Florian

