The IDE stuff is pretending to be SCSI for the sake of the kernel.
Tru64 just treats it as a kind of broken SCSI interface only capable of having 2
devices.
As for the hwmgr thing, are you sure that the text says what you think it says?
I think that it says that the drive has a device id of 1 (This isn't the same of as
the SCSI ID). Look at the first valid path to the device (in square brackets at
the end of the line) I bet it has the bus device lun information you thought you'd
find.

Hope this helps
Adam





