Hi, Peter!

You can also use rsh to perform remote backups! In fact, I've never
tryied the syntax you showed.

I use the following syntax to do this job!

dump:
-----
# find / -print | cpio -ocvB | rsh host_with_tape dd of=/dev/rmt0h

list:
-----
# rsh host_with_tape dd if=/dev/rmt0h | cpio -itv

restore:
--------
# rsh host_with_tape dd if=/dev/rmt0h | cpio -idvcumB

I hope it helps you!

