> These Volumes all reside on diffrent Subdisks.
> ! These Subdisks are all striped over the same four disks !

Sounds as if you've created an "actuator-contention" configuration.
I would recommend you understand which datafiles (and redo logs
and rollback segments) consume the most bandwidth and require the
quickest access, then approach your striping exercise from there.

With a small number of physical disks, striping can actually hurt
rather than help because the database sees fewer number of "virtual
actuators" and therefore spends lots of time waiting for I/Os
which now are serialized through a smaller funnel.  This would
apply to most all systems but especially transaction-oriented ones
where it is mandatory to have many concurrent unthrottled I/Os.


