> Does anybody know how to setup superuser access for a non-privilege
> user?

Depends on what you want to do.

If you want a user to have full superuser access, but be able to
track what they're doing with audit, you could set up a second 
account with uid 0, have them su to this account for superuser 
access.

If you want a user to be able to do one thing that requires root
access, you could write a program that executes this thing, make
it setuid root, and set it to be executable only by the given user.

If you want some users to be able to do some things that require
root access, you should look into "dop" (available on the system,
starting with V5.0 or thereabouts) or "sudo" (freeware).


