    # The way CDE decides to run the user's .xsession file is determined in 
    # /usr/dt/bin/Xsession.  In DEC UNIX, the default behavior is different 
    # from the others (it would run the .xsession file if the file exists).
    # We have modified /usr/dt/bin/Xsession on the DEC UNIX systems so that 
    # it conforms with the other UNIX systems.  The modification is to change
    # the line
    #   if [ "$SESSIONTYPE" = "xdm" -o "$SESSIONTYPE" = "dx" ]; then 
    # to
    #   if [ "$SESSIONTYPE" = "xdm" ]; then
    # Only "root" can do this.

