If I understand your question correctly,
If a patch has ever been installed in your system, there then a utility
called dupatch is probably also installed. (defaults to
/usr/sbin/dupatch)
If there is no dupatch on your system, chances are no patches have been
installed.
If there is dupatch, u can use this syntax:
#dupatch -track -type patch
and this should list all patches installed in your system.

Or else, manually, if not deleted, u should find something in
/var/adm/patch  and look at the logs.
Hope this helps.



