I'm not sure I understand the question, since it seems so obvious

        /abc {

will find a line with "abc {" in it.  If you want a regular expression,
then:

        /abc.*{                         # anything between 'c' and '{'
or
        /[a-z][a-z0-9_]*.*{             # any alphanumeric 
or
        /abc[   ][      ]*{             # 'abc' white space '{'
or
        /[a-z][a-z0-9_][        ][      ]*{     # alphanumeric white
                                                # space '{'

are all regular expressions that should find "abc {"

The man page for 'ed' says look at the 'grep' command man page for an
explanation of what regular expressions are supported in 'ed'.

