I don't have an Admin guide at hand, so I don't know if it's mentioned there.
But, did you write an Advfs bootblock on the disk using the disklabel(8)
command?  See the man page for disklabel for details.

Basically, what you're going to want to do is to boot to the distribution
CDROM, use the disklabel command fix your disk.  I haven't tried the following
sequence of commands, but it's something like this:

#
# Start by getting the current label.  Change rrz0a to be your 
# system disk.
#
disklabel -r /dev/rrz0a > /tmp/rz0.label
#
# Now, restore that label, but also specify the type of boot
# blocks we want.  Change rrz0a to be your system disk
# and change RZ28 to be the type of disk it is. 
#
disklabel -Rr -t advfs /dev/rrz0a /tmp/rz0.label RZ28

        Stu


