In article <9d07t5$9f6$1@unlisys.unlisys.net> "sake" <sake@snafu.de> writes:
>I have implemented a root Partition with advfs. I have
>rebuild the /etc/fdmns dir so that the root_domain  points
>to the right disk.
>
>Concerning the Admin Guide i have done everything correct
>but when i boot from consol prompt i get the error message
>osf-boot could not be opened.
>
>So it seems that the Alpha can't read from a advfs partition.
>Does anyone has a clue to what the problem here is.

If you got the message "cannot open osf_boot", it means that the
filesystem on your root partition didn't contain the osf_boot executable.
The primary bootstrap blocks are in place (they are what issued that
message), but the secondary bootstrap program, osf_boot, isn't.

Can you boot another disk and mount this root partition? If so, see
if there is an osf_boot (there likely isn't). Copy one over from another
disk of the same O/S release.

