Mikhail Isayev wrote:

> I got some strange problem analyzing core files on Tru64. Both dbx and
> ladebug show stack trace OK, if I run them on the same box there the
> core has occured.  If the box is different stack trace is full with
> garbage.

What's probably happened is that your two "boxes" also have different
versions of the operating system installed, with different shared
libraries. (They may even APPEAR to have the same version, from "uname"
or even "sizer -v", but have different patch levels of one or more
library.) If so, it's not the "stack trace" that's broken, but the
attempt by the debugger to find NAMES for the addresses in the stack
trace, because the code has moved around between versions.

