:    the TCP/IP layer. Can this be done on a DS20E running Tru64 4.0f ?
:    If so, do we need any hardware to make it happen (Eg. WIC),
:    or is it possible to do with software and a nic ?

CISCO-B can translate X.25 to TCP/IP (see "protocol translation" section in
CISCO doc).
Then for terminal access from DS20E to HOST, you can simply telnet
to CISCO-B (to the IP address and port, whitch is configured in protocol
translation).
If you need terminal access from HOST to DS20E, you can start X.25 sesion
and CISCO-B start telnet to the DS20E.
For this application no X.25 hardware for DS20E required.

