We ran a couple of AlphaServers with 100Mbps Full Duplex under v4.0d 
for several years with no problems. It sounds to me as if the other end
(ie. the hub or switch) needs investigating. I would guess it is set to
autonegotiate the speed and duplex setting, and my experience is that a
good fraction of the time, the autonegotiation gets the speed right but
sets half duplex when the other end is set to full duplex. This causes
appalling performance and it is not obvious that this is the cause 
unless you've seen the effect before. I generally find it better to
disable autonegotiation at both ends.
Hope this helps.

John Hill 

