"Dr. J.C.Hill" <hill@hep.phy.cam.ac.uk> writes:

> andrew.rycroft@intrinsitech.com wrote:
>> 
>> What is the earliest version of Tru64UNIX that supports
>> 100Mbits/sec full duplex ethenret communication ? We are running a
>> Tru64UNIX v4.0d system, and when we tried to run at 100Mbit/sec
>> full duplex we had all sorts of network problems. If we run at half
>> duplex then it runs fine. We are using a DE500 cards, and set the
>> EWA0_MODE parameter to FAST, or FASTFD.
>> 
> We ran a couple of AlphaServers with 100Mbps Full Duplex under v4.0d
> for several years with no problems. It sounds to me as if the other
> end (ie. the hub or switch) needs investigating. 

DE500 io-cards needed a driver included in patch #4 i think.
DU v4.0E is ok out of the box for these cards.

The DE600s is not supported under DU v4.0F on A1000s as I recall.

> I would guess it is set to autonegotiate the speed and duplex
> setting, and my experience is that a good fraction of the time, the
> autonegotiation gets the speed right but sets half duplex when the
> other end is set to full duplex. This causes appalling performance
> and it is not obvious that this is the cause unless you've seen the
> effect before. I generally find it better to disable autonegotiation
> at both ends. 

On DU v4.0x - up to "F" "ewa0_mode=FastFD" was "right" for us -
lately auto has been starting to work better. On v5.1s as well.

Regards,
